{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>After he hears.</b> After he heard and upheld it — having said 'it is possible for me,' then went back and annulled it for her, even on that very day." "<b>And he shall bear her iniquity.</b> He enters in her stead. We learn from here that one who causes a stumbling to his fellow enters in his stead for all punishments."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:19.503526346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}